# Using Different Domains

You can also serve locales under different domains:

```js
module.exports = {
  i18n: {
    locales: ['en', 'fr'],
    defaultLocale: 'en',
    domains: [
      { domain: 'example.com', defaultLocale: 'en' },
      { domain: 'example.fr', defaultLocale: 'fr' },
    ],
  },
};
```

Now `example.com` serves English, `example.fr` serves French. Next.js handles the mapping.
